-- title:
--   Uniqueness of a reduction map on places of X_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Fix $M \ge 1$ and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and write $\Gamma = \Gamma_H(M)$ for the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained as the image under the inclusion $\Gamma_0(M) \hookrightarrow \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H$ under the character $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ sending a matrix to the class of its lower-right entry. Let $p$ be a prime with $p \nmid M$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, with residue field $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$. For a field $K$ let $F_K \subseteq K((q))$ be the $K$-subfield generated by the ratios $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma$ (denominator non-zero), and let $E \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ be the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of $F_{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $r_1, r_2$ be two maps from the set of places of $E/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (valuation subrings of $E$, proper, containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with principal ideals) to the places of $F_{\kappa}/\kappa$. Assume of each $r_i$: for every $y \in A((q))$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ lies in $E$ and whose coefficientwise reduction lies in $F_{\kappa}$ and is non-zero, and every divisor $D$ on $E$ with $D(P) = \mathrm{ord}_P(y)$ for all places $P$, the pushforward $\mathrm{mapDomain}\,r_i\,D$ takes the value $\mathrm{ord}_Q$ of the reduction of $y$ at every place $Q$ of $F_{\kappa}$. Then $r_1 = r_2$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of Deuring's reduction of the function field of $X_H(M)$ at a place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above a prime $p \nmid M$: a map on places is pinned down by the requirement that it carry divisors of $A$-integral $q$-expansions to the divisors of their reductions. It is used in the identification of the place attached to a point of the model of $X_H$ at $p$ with the specialisation of a place along the reduction map.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_placeReduction_unique_of_forall_mapDomain_eq_ord_gammaH_of_not_dvd.lean

